{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":387652,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"fd2b0a64-2a0b-4524-bad3-2e851073eced","total_cost_usd":1.4483685,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":65763,"cache_read_input_tokens":16967,"output_tokens":29449,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":65763,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":29449,"cache_read_input_tokens":16967,"cache_creation_input_tokens":65763,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":65763},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":45915,"outputTokens":21,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.04602,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":29449,"cacheReadInputTokens":16967,"cacheCreationInputTokens":65763,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.4023485,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\n  \"agent\": \"playtester\",\n  \"verdict\": \"targets_missed\",\n  \"summary\": \"The config cannot reach a single band — all three ascents crashed with 0 kg of fuel left — and the two halves of the reentry sweep disagree by 30 heat points about the same flight, so every heat-shield gating claim in the params rests on a number the simulator contradicts; the aerobraking optimum itself is real but mis-priced, because one skim array was adopted for all three bands when the measured per-band arrays put the optimum at 3 passes everywhere, inside the GDD's 2-4 window.\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ascent_fails_from_every_band\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.6\",\n      \"claim\": \"game_params balance_notes: 4000 m/s exhaust velocity on a 620 kg tank over 1200 kg dry gives 1666 m/s, enough for the suborbital band at ~1350 m/s with losses and the low band at ~1430 m/s 'with no margin', leaving ~315 m/s of reserve.\",\n      \"measured\": \"All three ascents failed: suborbital (102,500 m), low (170,000 m) and high (275,000 m) all report reached=false, why='crashed on ascent', fuel_remaining_kg=0, fuel_margin_pct=0. The flown loss budget exceeds the estimate by more than the entire claimed reserve. The grid says this is recoverable, not structural: bands_reachable is satisfied by 57.7% of 324 configurations and by all 12 best-scoring ones, though fuel_margin_sane is the second-least satisfiable target in the whole space at 32.7%.\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"heat_scale_inconsistent_between_experiments\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"claim\": \"The sweep states its own normalisation: 'an empty ship making a single-pass descent from the suborbital band peaks at 100'. The params build the entire upgrade gate on it — heat_index 100 / 126.6 / 157.1 against heat_capacity 100, heat_shield t1 at 135 and t2 at 175.\",\n      \"measured\": \"The two experiments report that same nominal flight differently. The skims series at entry_depth 0 gives suborbital empty, 0 skims = 100.0 peak (the calibration point). The descents table gives suborbital, empty, passes=1 = peak_heat 70 at a braking altitude of 55,602.6 m. That is a 30-point disagreement on one flight, so heat_index and the descents' peak_heat column are not on the same scale and cannot both be right. Every 'which heat shield tier does this band need' claim depends on which one is.\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"single_skim_array_mis_prices_two_of_three_bands\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"claim\": \"ablation.skim_heat_multiplier is one array, [1.0, 0.971, 0.944, 0.918], adopted from the high band and applied to all three; the resulting cost_curve puts optimal_skims at 0 / 1 / 2, i.e. 1 / 2 / 3 total passes. GDD 2.3.1 requires the cheapest descent to be 2-4 committed passes, 'never a single plunge'.\",\n      \"measured\": \"The measured arrays differ sharply by band: suborbital [1, 0.898, 0.730, 0.730], low [1, 0.956, 0.912, 0.867], high [1, 0.971, 0.944, 0.918]. Re-running the params' own ablation formula (base 0.56, growth 1.8, coefficient 1e-5, exponent 3, skim_peak 30) against the measured arrays gives suborbital [10.56, 9.08, 7.81, 11.35] and low [20.85, 19.57, 19.31, 20.68] — optimum 2 skims, i.e. 3 total passes, in both, and 3 passes in the high band as already priced. So the flown physics puts the optimum at 3 / 3 / 3, inside the GDD window, and the adopted array is what moves the suborbital band to a single plunge. It is the largest single error in the file: the suborbital plunge is priced at 10.56% of plate when the measured optimum is 7.81%, a 26% overcharge that erases the shipping slice's first band's only aerobraking decision.\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"unstaged_shallow_pass_unsurvivable_from_suborbital\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"claim\": \"GDD 2.3.1: 'shallow unstaged passes are survivable because cargo damage only begins at 100% heat', and the intended descent is coarse braking with the naked hull before staging, with thrust still available to reshape the periapsis between passes.\",\n      \"measured\": \"unstaged_braking: suborbital shallow pass peak heat 407 against heat_capacity 100 — 4.1x over the cargo-damage line, survivable=false. Low band 93, survivable=true. The intended pre-stage braking sequence therefore does not exist from the band the semester slice ships first, and the ordering is inverted (the lower, slower band is four times hotter than the higher one). The grid says this is structural, not a knob: unstaged_pass_survivable is satisfied by only 13.0% of 324 configurations, the least achievable of the eight targets, and no configuration in the space scores 8/8.\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\",\n      \"kind\": \"design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"skimming_and_unstaged_survival_are_mutually_exclusive\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"4.5\",\n      \"claim\": \"GDD 2.3.1 asks for both: shallow unstaged passes that survive, and skims that meaningfully cool the committed entry. The design treats them as two halves of one descent.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Best score across all 324 grid worlds is 7 of 8; nothing reaches 8. In every one of the 12 best-scoring configurations, exactly one of skimming_cools_the_entry and unstaged_pass_survivable is false, and the split tracks ballistic coefficient: the configs where skims bite hard run beta 44.4-133.3 with unstaged peaks of 339-439, while every config with a survivable unstaged pass (35-70) runs beta 400-1333 and skim multipliers of 0.976-0.993 per skim, i.e. no skim benefit at all. Satisfaction rates confirm it: skimming_cools_the_entry 43.8%, unstaged_pass_survivable 13.0%. Separately, all 12 best configurations sit at radius 60,000 m with a 16,800 m atmosphere — none at 160,000 or 320,000 m, the two grid points that bracket the crew's 250,000 m planet.\",\n      \"severity\": \"significant\",\n      \"kind\": \"design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"descents_experiment_holds_one_depth\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"claim\": \"The descents table reports cheapest_pass_count = 1 in all nine band x load cases and would, read at face value, settle GDD 4.5 risk 1 as confirmed: the U-curve has no left arm and a single plunge is always cheapest.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Ablation rises monotonically with pass count everywhere — suborbital empty 4.1 / 5.0 / 5.6 / 6.2 / 6.8 / 11.3, high full hold 7.7 / 11.3 / 12.3 / 13.0 up to 24.1 at 23 passes — and so does peak heat (suborbital empty 70 / 73 / 73 / 74; high full hold 89 / 96 / 98 / 99 / 103). Extra passes getting hotter is the signature of a single-periapsis experiment: braking_altitude_m climbs with pass count (suborbital empty 55,602 to 74,790) but there is no separate committed-entry depth, so this table cannot show the two-depth descent the GDD describes and its pass optimum is not evidence about the ablation curve. The skims table, which does hold a committed entry at a fixed depth, shows the opposite sign — heat falls with skims in all three bands. This is the exact conflation the charter warns of, reproduced in the current sweep.\",\n      \"severity\": \"significant\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"skims_cost_more_than_the_plate_they_save\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"claim\": \"The ablation curve is tuned so that a planned sequence of committed passes is 'the cheap path', with the cost expressed in shield plate at replate_cost_per_pct 2.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Priced in plate alone the optimum is real but shallow: high band 36.54 at 2 skims against 39.33 direct — 2.79 points, 5.6 credits — and low band 0.44 points as currently priced (1.54 against the measured array). Priced in everything else it is negative. From the skims table, the 2-skim high-band descent costs commit_dv of 46 + 47 = 93 m/s and the low-band one 51 + 52 = 103 m/s, against the ~315 m/s of post-circularisation reserve the params claim — a third of the entire budget — and it costs 1.83 hours of in-world time at the high band (1.41 h direct vs 3.24 h) and 1.49 h at the low band, on orbital periods of 44-80 minutes that already make >=100x time warp a hard requirement. The player spends a third of the reserve and two hours to save five credits.\",\n      \"severity\": \"significant\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"no_heat_margin_at_base_gear\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"claim\": \"The balance notes state plainly that a base-gear direct suborbital entry 'reads exactly 100 against reentry.heat_capacity 100, i.e. it sits on the cargo-damage line', and calls that a decision rather than a defect.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Confirmed at 100.0 exactly, with zero margin — and the simulator is the most forgiving pilot the game will ever have. off_retrograde_penalty is 1 in the params and the model carries no attitude error at all, so the cosine term GDD 2.3.1 requires is never exercised; any real off-retrograde drift puts the base configuration over the line on the game's first band. On the descents scale the same picture holds at greed: suborbital full hold, single pass peaks at 98, and every full-hold descent at 2 or more passes exceeds 100 in every band (suborbital 101-103, low 99-103, high 96-103).\",\n      \"severity\": \"significant\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cargo_mass_per_slot_not_reproducible\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.5\",\n      \"claim\": \"balance_notes report 170.89 kg per slot, a 1025.3 kg six-slot hold and a 1.854x mass ratio as 'the flown figure ... because that is the number the simulator can reproduce', with 173.5 / 1041.0 / 1.868 offered only as a caveat against the shipped catalog.\",\n      \"measured\": \"The simulator flew the caveat, not the headline: kg_per_slot 173.48, full_hold_kg 1040.9, full_hold_mass_ratio 1.87. The mechanical claim survives — 1.87x is 'roughly doubles' per GDD 2.3.5 either way — but the number the params single out as reproducible is the one the sweep does not reproduce.\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"full_hold_descent_speed_claim_is_circular\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.2\",\n      \"claim\": \"landing.descent_speed_full_hold_ms is 4.18, described as the flown value, with parachute_drag_coefficient 1.8 unchanged 'since 4.18 is what it flies'.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Measured touchdown is 4.04 m/s at full hold in all three bands (3.54 half hold, 2.96 empty) — within 3.4% of the claim and comfortably under the 5 m/s soft line, so the target holds. But the sweep had to solve for a parachute area of 610.5 m2 from descent_speed_full_hold_ms itself because landing.parachute_area_m2 does not exist in the params, so the measurement is anchored to the claim it appears to confirm and is not independent evidence. Touchdown speed is identical across bands at equal mass, which does confirm that descent speed is mass-driven only, as designed.\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"proposed_changes\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"flight.fuel_capacity_kg\",\n      \"current\": 620,\n      \"proposed\": 900,\n      \"reason\": \"Raises ideal delta-v from 4000*ln(1820/1200)=1666 m/s to 4000*ln(2100/1200)=2238 m/s so the ascent that crashed from all three bands has real margin; costs launch TWR (16000/8400 = 1.90, still above 1) and forces the fuel_tank upgrade ladder up above the new base.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"ablation.skim_heat_multiplier\",\n      \"current\": [1, 0.971, 0.944, 0.918],\n      \"proposed\": {\n        \"suborbital\": [1, 0.898, 0.73, 0.73],\n        \"low\": [1, 0.956, 0.912, 0.867],\n        \"high\": [1, 0.971, 0.944, 0.918]\n      },\n      \"reason\": \"One array cannot be within tolerance of both 0.730 and 0.944 at index 2, and adopting the high band's flattens the suborbital band's skim decision entirely; costs a schema change in schemas/game-params.schema.json, which the Economy Balancer flagged it could not make from where it sits.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"ablation.optimal_skims\",\n      \"current\": {\"suborbital\": 0, \"low\": 1, \"high\": 2},\n      \"proposed\": {\"suborbital\": 2, \"low\": 2, \"high\": 2},\n      \"reason\": \"Re-running the params' own formula against the measured per-band arrays puts the optimum at 2 skims (3 total passes) in every band, inside GDD 2.3.1's 2-4 window; costs nothing but the claim that the bands differ in optimal pass count.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"ablation.cost_curve\",\n      \"current\": {\"suborbital\": [10.56, 10.99, 12.33, 15.19], \"low\": [20.85, 20.41, 20.99, 23.16], \"high\": [39.33, 37.33, 36.54, 37.45]},\n      \"proposed\": {\"suborbital\": [10.56, 9.08, 7.81, 11.35], \"low\": [20.85, 19.57, 19.31, 20.68], \"high\": [39.33, 37.33, 36.54, 37.45]},\n      \"reason\": \"Recomputed from the per-band arrays with every other ablation coefficient untouched, which deepens the suborbital decision from nothing to 2.75 points of plate; costs the reported saving in the low band, which shrinks from a claimed 0.44 to a genuine 1.54 measured against a corrected direct entry.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"reentry.heat_capacity\",\n      \"current\": 100,\n      \"proposed\": 112,\n      \"reason\": \"Gives the base-gear direct suborbital entry (measured 100.0) 12 points of headroom for the attitude error the simulator does not model, while preserving both upgrade gates exactly — low at 126.6 still needs heat_shield t1's 135 and high at 157.1 still needs t2's 175; costs the knife-edge the Balancer chose deliberately.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"baseline.reentry.reference_area_m2\",\n      \"current\": 3.5,\n      \"proposed\": 6.0,\n      \"reason\": \"Moves staged ballistic coefficient from 228.6 to 133.3, into the range where the grid's skimming_cools_the_entry target is actually satisfied (best configs at 44.4 and 133.3 satisfy it; every one at 400-1333 fails it), which is the only lever that widens the shallow optimum; costs unstaged survivability, already the least achievable target in the space at 13.0%, and puts the ship below Apollo's 350-390 kg/m2 that the Researcher's derivation anchored to.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"upgrades[0].value\",\n      \"current\": 800,\n      \"proposed\": 1150,\n      \"reason\": \"fuel_tank t1 has to sit above the new 900 kg base or the first purchase is a downgrade; costs a slightly larger jump in reach at tier 1.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"upgrades[1].value\",\n      \"current\": 1000,\n      \"proposed\": 1400,\n      \"reason\": \"Keeps the fuel_tank ladder monotone above the retuned t1; costs nothing else, since band gating is set by the base tank.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"landing.parachute_area_m2\",\n      \"current\": null,\n      \"proposed\": 610.5,\n      \"reason\": \"The sweep had to solve for this from descent_speed_full_hold_ms, so the descent-speed claim currently validates itself; stating the area makes it falsifiable and costs one field.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"confidence_notes\": [\n    \"The heat-scale contradiction is the finding I would resolve before acting on any other. The sweep's stated calibration flight (empty, suborbital, single pass) reads 100.0 in the skims table and 70 in the descents table. I trust the skims series because it holds the committed entry at a fixed depth while the descents table lets a search pick braking_altitude_m per pass count, and depth is the largest single lever on heat. If that judgement is backwards, then the descents table is authoritative and the band difficulty ordering is inverted rather than merely mis-measured — cheapest ablation falls 4.1 / 3.6 / 3.2 empty and 10.0 / 8.7 / 7.7 full hold as altitude rises, and peak heat falls 70 / 67 / 64 — which would make GDD 4.5 risk 2 a live blocking failure instead of an artifact. I am not calling it that on evidence this self-contradictory.\",\n    \"The ascent failures report only 'crashed' with 0 kg remaining and no peak altitude, so I cannot measure the shortfall. The 900 kg figure is the rocket equation plus a margin, not a measured requirement; re-fly the ascent before committing to it, and have the harness report apoapsis reached so the next pass can size the tank rather than guess at it.\",\n    \"The simulator is a point mass with a perfect pilot: no attitude error, so the cosine term GDD 2.3.1 requires is never exercised and off_retrograde_penalty of 1 is untested; no debris collisions; and no EVA, tether, magnet-shear or compactor model at all, so every claim in §2.3.4 and every EVA number in the params is unverified by this sweep and should not be read as confirmed by it.\",\n    \"The delta-v cost I price against the skim decision assumes the propellant is scarce. Fuel still in the tank at staging is jettisoned, so a skim's 46-52 m/s is free if the player was going to throw it away — the cost is real only when it eats the reserve needed to reach the band at all, which on the current tank (and certainly on the crashed ascent) it does.\",\n    \"The exploration grid does not contain the crew's planet. Radius options are 800, 60,000, 160,000 and 320,000 m and the flown world is 250,000 m, so satisfaction rates and the beta thresholds I quote are directional rather than a verdict on this planet specifically. The 800 m corner is degenerate and is counted in all 324 denominators, which makes every satisfaction rate slightly pessimistic.\",\n    \"Nothing here says whether any of it is fun. The corrected optimum saves 26% of plate at the suborbital band and 7% at the low band, and I can say those are decisions arithmetically; whether two extra orbits under time warp reads as a plan or as a chore is Checkpoint 2, and the shallow high-band margin in particular may feel like nothing in the hands even after the per-band arrays land.\"\n  ]\n}","ttft_ms":304447,"ttft_stream_ms":3195,"time_to_request_ms":193,"type":"result","duration_ms":385387,"uuid":"78c1cfe1-3536-4f5e-a493-7c59585ce065"}
